Package: golang-github-katzenpost-hpqc-dev
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: hybrid post-quantum cryptography for Katzenpost (Go source)
 hpqc provides the KEM, NIKE, signature, hash and BACAP primitives the
 Katzenpost mix network is built on, combining classical and post-quantum
 constructions.
 .
 This package ships the Go source for use as a build dependency. It
 contains no compiled code, so no Go toolchain newer than the archive's
 own is required to build it.

Package: python3-hpqc
Section: python
Architecture: all
Depends: ${python3:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         python3-highctidh
Description: hpqc for Python
 A Python implementation of hpqc, which provides the KEM, NIKE,
 signature, hash and BACAP primitives the Katzenpost mix network is built
 on, combining traditional and post-quantum constructions. It produces
 the same bytes as the Go implementation rather than wrapping it.
